    "question": {
      "dom_id": "question-174367",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A={m,r,t}$ of $X={m,n,r,s,t}.$",
      "worked_solution": "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)={\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set ${m,r,t}$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114807/assets/1fd2100d57c3483e737dc40298d4d5f61099ebc2863c54839906b66183acf576.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $m,r$ and $t$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
